Keep your core React app unchanged. Store in DB whether a page is dynamic or custom.
For custom pages, create a separate React app, run npm run build, and host/copy the built JS & CSS (S3, CDN, Nginx, or core app public folder).
When core app reads a custom page config from DB, it dynamically loads the bundle and mounts it inside a div in the main panel, passing inputs as JSON props.
The custom app exposes a global mount() function and can also send data back via callbacks.


